{"id":"h238","run":2,"role":"test_wrong","category":"science-chemistry","question":"A chemical reaction takes place in a container of cross-sectional area $50 \\mathrm{~cm}^2$. As a result of the reaction, a piston is pushed out through $15 \\mathrm{~cm}$ against an external pressure of $1.0 \\mathrm{~atm}$. Calculate the work done by the system.\nIs the correct answer \"-75 $\\mathrm{~J}$\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"no","correct":false,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The work done by the system is negative because the system does work on the surroundings as the piston moves out.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":2.0234},{"text":"The work is given by w = −P_ext·ΔV.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4923,"phi":2.6753},{"text":"The volume change is 50 cm² × 15 cm = 750 cm³ = 7.50×10⁻⁴ m³.","confidence":0.97,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.5237,"phi":2.7906},{"text":"Using 1 atm = 1.01325×10⁵ Pa, the work is about −76.0 J.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":2.8795},{"text":"Since 1 atm·L = 101.3 J, 0.750 L·atm is about 76.0 J.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":2.9578},{"text":"The magnitude 75 J is close and arises from multiplying 1 atm by 750 cm³ with loose rounding.","confidence":0.6,"lean":1,"theta":0.9425,"phi":-0.0871},{"text":"The −75 J value results from loose rounding of the conversion factor and does not match the precise result.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":2.9793},{"text":"The correct answer is −76 J, not −75 J.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":2.9312}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.2,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"su